<title>JAPAN: BOJ sees May money market surplus of 4.31 trln yen.</title>
<headline>BOJ sees May money market surplus of 4.31 trln yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's money market is expected to have a 4.31 trillion yen surplus in May, down from a 7.0785 trillion yen surplus a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>Of the total, bank notes are expected to be in surplus by 2.2 trillion yen, against a surplus of 2.3976 trillion yen a year earlier.</p>
<p>Details, excluding expected government bond issues, are as follows (in billions of yen; figures may not tally due to rounding):  </p>
<p>						   May 97	May 96</p>
<p> Bank Notes				    +2,200    +2,397.6</p>
<p> Fiscal Funds				  +2,110    +4,680.9</p>
<p>    Redemption of government bonds     +3,110    +3,090.2</p>
<p>    Taxes					-3,350    -3,354.8</p>
<p>    Social security			    +840	+825.4</p>
<p>    Public works				 +530	+507.1</p>
<p>    Grants to local governments	     -10	+152.5</p>
<p>    Other general accounts		   +420	+467.4</p>
<p>    Insurance				  -2,970    -2,774.9</p>
<p>    Public finance corporation	     +400	+752.1</p>
<p>    Others					 +570	+410.0</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------  Total					   +4,310    +7,078.5</p>
</text>
